<article class="env-lemma" id="07NH">
       
      
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07NH">Lemma <span data-tag="07NH">10.166.3</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a field. Let $A \to B$ be a faithfully flat $k$-algebra map. If $B$ is geometrically regular over $k$, so is $A$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Assume $B$ is geometrically regular over $k$. Let $k'/k$ be a finite, purely inseparable extension. Then $A \otimes _ k k' \to B \otimes _ k k'$ is faithfully flat as a base change of $A \to B$ (by Lemmas <a href="/tag/00FI" data-tag="00FI">10.30.3</a> and <a href="/tag/00HI" data-tag="00HI">10.39.7</a>) and $B \otimes _ k k'$ is regular by our assumption on $B$ over $k$. Then $A \otimes _ k k'$ is regular by Lemma <a href="/tag/07NG" data-tag="07NG">10.164.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>